Pros/Cons:
Pros	Cons
No dependency conflicts	Loses validation & type safety
Simpler debugging	Manual error checking required
Faster startup time	No auto-documentation
Works with any container runtime	Less maintainable for complex config
This approach removes all Pydantic-related complexity while maintaining the core functionality. It's particularly useful if you're experiencing dependency version conflicts or validation-related startup issues.
